{"id":"119-s-6","label":"S. 6","congress":119,"title":"Born-Alive Abortion Survivors Protection Act","latestVote":"2025-01-22","rollIds":["Senate:1:11"],"hasMetadata":true,"chambers":["Senate"],"congressUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/6","metadataUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/bulkdata/BILLSTATUS/119/s/BILLSTATUS-119s6.xml","metadata":{"title":"Born-Alive Abortion Survivors Protection Act","introduced":"2025-01-15","latestAction":"Cloture on the motion to proceed to the measure not invoked in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 52 - 47. Record Vote Number: 11. (CR S294-295)","latestActionDate":"2025-01-22","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","subjects":["Abortion","Civil actions and liability","Criminal investigation, prosecution, interrogation","Health personnel","Legal fees and court costs","Medical ethics","Violent crime"],"sponsors":["Sen. Lankford, James [R-OK]"],"cosponsors":["Sen. Banks, Jim [R-IN]","Sen. Thune, John [R-SD]","Sen. Hyde-Smith, Cindy [R-MS]","Sen. Risch, James E. [R-ID]","Sen. Lummis, Cynthia M. [R-WY]","Sen. Britt, Katie Boyd [R-AL]","Sen. McConnell, Mitch [R-KY]","Sen. Wicker, Roger F. [R-MS]","Sen. Blackburn, Marsha [R-TN]","Sen. Crapo, Mike [R-ID]","Sen. Fischer, Deb [R-NE]","Sen. Grassley, Chuck [R-IA]","Sen. Hoeven, John [R-ND]","Sen. Marshall, Roger [R-KS]","Sen. Tillis, Thomas [R-NC]","Sen. Budd, Ted [R-NC]","Sen. Scott, Tim [R-SC]","Sen. Johnson, Ron [R-WI]","Sen. Sheehy, Tim [R-MT]","Sen. Tuberville, Tommy [R-AL]","Sen. Hagerty, Bill [R-TN]","Sen. Curtis, John R. [R-UT]","Sen. Young, Todd [R-IN]","Sen. Ricketts, Pete [R-NE]","Sen. Cramer, Kevin [R-ND]","Sen. Barrasso, John [R-WY]","Sen. Kennedy, John [R-LA]","Sen. Cornyn, John [R-TX]","Sen. Cassidy, Bill [R-LA]","Sen. Rounds, Mike [R-SD]","Sen. Ernst, Joni [R-IA]","Sen. Scott, Rick [R-FL]","Sen. Daines, Steve [R-MT]","Sen. Mullin, Markwayne [R-OK]","Sen. Graham, Lindsey [R-SC]","Sen. Cruz, Ted [R-TX]","Sen. Schmitt, Eric [R-MO]","Sen. Lee, Mike [R-UT]","Sen. Sullivan, Dan [R-AK]","Sen. Moran, Jerry [R-KS]","Sen. Cotton, Tom [R-AR]","Sen. Hawley, Josh [R-MO]","Sen. McCormick, David [R-PA]","Sen. Boozman, John [R-AR]","Sen. Moreno, Bernie [R-OH]","Sen. Capito, Shelley Moore [R-WV]","Sen. Moody, Ashley [R-FL]","Sen. Paul, Rand [R-KY]","Sen. Justice, James C. [R-WV]","Sen. Graham, Darline [R-SC]"],"committees":[],"laws":[],"committeeReports":[],"costEstimates":[],"relatedBills":[{"title":"Born-Alive Abortion Survivors Protection Act","relationship":"Related bill","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/21"}],"textVersions":[{"date":"2025-01-16","stage":"Placed on Calendar Senate","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/BILLS-119s6pcs/xml/BILLS-119s6pcs.xml"}],"summaries":[{"date":"2025-01-15","stage":"Introduced in Senate","text":"Born-Alive Abortion Survivors Protection Act\n\nThis bill establishes requirements for the degree of care a health care practitioner must provide in the case of a child born alive following an abortion or attempted abortion.\n\nSpecifically, a health care practitioner who is present must (1) exercise the same degree of care as would reasonably be provided to any other child born alive at the same gestational age, and (2) ensure the child is immediately admitted to a hospital. Additionally, a health care practitioner or other employee who has knowledge of a failure to comply with the degree-of-care requirements must immediately report such failure to law enforcement.\n\nA health care practitioner who fails to provide the required degree of care, or a health care practitioner or other employee who fails to report such failure, is subject to criminal penalties—a fine, up to five years in prison, or both.\n\nAn individual who intentionally kills or attempts to kill a child born alive is subject to prosecution for murder.\n\nThe bill bars the criminal prosecution of a mother of a child born alive under this bill and allows her to bring a civil action against a health care practitioner or other employee for violations."}],"actions":[{"date":"2025-01-22","text":"Cloture on the motion to proceed to the measure not invoked in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 52 - 47. Record Vote Number: 11. (CR S294-295)"},{"date":"2025-01-22","text":"Motion to proceed to measure considered in Senate. (CR S283)"},{"date":"2025-01-21","text":"Motion to proceed to measure considered in Senate. (CR S275-276)"},{"date":"2025-01-20","text":"Cloture motion on the motion to proceed to the measure presented in Senate. (CR S258)"},{"date":"2025-01-20","text":"Motion to proceed to consideration of measure made in Senate. (CR S258)"},{"date":"2025-01-16","text":"Read the second time. Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under General Orders. Calendar No. 4."},{"date":"2025-01-15","text":"Introduced in the Senate. Read the first time. Placed on Senate Legislative Calendar under Read the First Time."},{"date":"2025-01-15","text":"Introduced in Senate"}]},"votes":[{"chamber":"Senate","congress":119,"session":1,"roll":11,"date":"2025-01-22","time":"02:38 PM","question":"On Cloture on the Motion to Proceed S. 6","description":"Motion to Invoke Cloture: Motion to Proceed to S.6","result":"Cloture on the Motion to Proceed Rejected (52-47, 3/5 majority required)","amendment":"","amendmentDetail":"","tieBreaker":"","url":"https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1191/vote_119_1_00011.htm","xmlUrl":"https://www.senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes/vote1191/vote_119_1_00011.xml","counts":{"yes":52,"no":47,"present":0,"notVoting":1},"members":[{"id":"S428","name":"Alsobrooks, Angela","state":"MD","party":"D","district":"","vote":"Nay","position":"no"},{"id":"S354","name":"Baldwin, Tammy","state":"WI","party":"D","district":"","vote":"Nay","position":"no"},{"id":"S429","name":"Banks, Jim","state":"IN","party":"R","district":"","vote":"Yea","position":"yes"},{"id":"S317","name":"Barrasso, John","state":"WY","party":"R","district":"","vote":"Yea","position":"yes"},{"id":